:"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ba3f82a0c10dbc62d1cfd7e7b8d0da9435b81b41441c2528f0cf7911b4eda023","event_uuid":"1cd69f38-2b93-4592-9241-81dc528e1e30","position":{"commit_sha":"0598b9bd961b474da3d79ea0adbdc43913409dce","position":"1786827719595673001-1cd69f38-2b93-4592-9241-81dc528e1e30"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"90352449df852875cd256abd8c0c5210a0049a9b6c131c5378519dc35ee41a5b","event_uuid":"a196be39-91a1-4f63-a7d7-b532c0c9e3d1","position":{"commit_sha":"e87b16d2243a875c4d7b0bff4603c3c9912fd219","position":"1786827728039647001-a196be39-91a1-4f63-a7d7-b532c0c9e3d1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786827626453128001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"e9ab25d9-e1cf-4fe9-a802-738afda1c18b","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"815d-8f56-7237-4b58"},{"link_uuid":"1cd69f38-2b93-4592-9241-81dc528e1e30","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ed2b-3262-fc64-4f69"},{"link_uuid":"a196be39-91a1-4f63-a7d7-b532c0c9e3d1","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"fa6e-78c8-f806-4283"}],"description":"## Context\ntest_cli_show_complete_or_erroring_under_write_burst costs 10.95-22.63s in recent CI samples and is the largest variable default-suite node. Closed slim-fetch-ledge is the original regression and must remain protected. Closed ambery-enigmatic-pussycat later added a generic table-driven reads-under-writer-storm property but intentionally retained the original show regression byte-for-byte. Runtime overlap alone does not prove redundancy.\n\n## Plan\n- Map both tests through the CLI, store read/reconvergence, writer process, output-completeness, exit-code, timeout, and cleanup paths.\n- Enumerate the original slim-fetch-ledge failure mechanism and any failure classes only the generic property reaches.\n- Seed each defect independently and run both oracles to establish a detection matrix.\n- If the generic property misses any original behavior, keep both or strengthen it under legitimate RED-to-GREEN before considering consolidation.\n- Measure repeated macOS and Ubuntu timings and compare concurrency-regression practice in maintained OSS projects.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The original empty-or-partial-success regression remains detectable through the real CLI.\n- [ ] Fault-seeded evidence shows which oracle detects every original and generic failure class.\n- [ ] Process concurrency, output completeness, exit status, timeout, and cleanup remain real.\n- [ ] Any consolidation removes an oracle only after behavioral equivalence is proven.\n- [ ] macOS wall and aggregate runner savings are measured.\n- [ ] slim-fetch-ledge, ambery-enigmatic-pussycat, and maintained OSS precedents are cited.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_show_no_stall.py","reason":"Original real-CLI write-burst regression oracle under equivalence analysis."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_reads_under_sync_contention.py","reason":"Generic table-driven read-under-contention property compared by fault seeding."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","ed2b-3262-fc64-4f69"],["relates_to","fa6e-78c8-f806-4283"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["ci","test-runtime","research","concurrency"],"ticket_id":"afa0-2e15-7db8-4d5b","ticket_type":"task","title":"Prove fault-seeded equivalence before consolidating show-under-write-burst regression","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["26e735b8-c4f7-4839-a693-0c8302ff14a4","03f203eb-0ad4-49f3-b589-4efd0877fec5","e9ab25d9-e1cf-4fe9-a802-738afda1c18b","1cd69f38-2b93-4592-9241-81dc528e1e30","a196be39-91a1-4f63-a7d7-b532c0c9e3d1"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786838726803009644,"uuid":"b0613aac-7c68-4f99-b558-23cc60fa9702"}